<body>
    <h1>Walk-me Variables - Operationalization</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><span style=3D"color:#0055cc;"><strong>CONSIDERATIONS:&nbsp;</st=
rong></span></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
 <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: 91=
.3594%;">
  <colgroup>
   <col style=3D"width: 8.74082%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 60.4021%;">
   <col style=3D"width: 30.8571%;">
  </colgroup>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><strong>Category</strong></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><strong>Details</strong></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><strong>Potential workaround</strong></p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Content setup</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Walk-me tool limitation:</em> <br>
       Styling breaks occur when walkthrough content is created by copying =
text from another source</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Type out content in walk-me instead of copying from an existing wor=
d/ power-point.<br>
       OR <br>
       Copy and paste the existing content to Notepad and from notepad past=
e the content in walk-me editor</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Content setup</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Walk-me tool limitation:</em> <br>
       Indentation/alignment breaks when hyperlinks are included as bullet =
points in walkthroughs</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>This is how walk-me works and this needs to be a consideration whil=
e setting up content</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Content configuration</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Walk-me tool limitation:</em><br>
       Walk-me supports only one tab in the Ireland menu configuration</p><=
/td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Content to be organized within this limitation till enhancements ar=
e completed</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Content maintenance</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><em>Walk-me tool limitation:</em><br>
       Changing the default styling (font, color, bold etc.) during content=
 creation of walkthroughs&nbsp; leads to CSS overwrite. <br>
       Hence future global future changes will not get applied to elements =
where default formatting was changed.<br><br>
       example- if you change the formatting of a popup header by increasin=
g the font size and few months down the line the default formatting of pop-=
up header is changed. Then these new styling will not get applied to header=
s where formatting changes were done during content creation. The changes i=
f required will then have to be done manually</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Consideration while setting up content</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Content configuration</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p><br></p>
     <p><em>Pop-up every time with frequency once/always - configuration</e=
m></p>
     <p>This setting should not be used else SSO users will see this pop-up=
 on the JIT screen.&nbsp;If this setting is used then additional segmentati=
on rules need to be applied to exclude SSO firms.&nbsp;Pls refer this ticke=
t for more details - &nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://jira.=
bnc.ca/browse/NBINPS-267" rel=3D"nofollow">NBINPS-267</a></p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>NA</p></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>SSO firms</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>For SSO firms the first-time user segment is not available</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">NA</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Out of Scope 1.0</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Walkthroughs will not work on modules that open in a different wind=
ow - Data export<br>
       Walk-me surveys and feedback forms were not part of styling and bran=
ding enhancements <br>
       Passing of variables between the R2 &amp; new Compass instance of Wa=
lk-me.</p>
     <p>Content management system for training materials</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Prod activations</p></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
     <p>Following need to be available for activating walk-me in Prod</p>
     <ol>
      <li>Content to be published in Prod</li>
      <li>CX launcher widget to be enabled</li>
     </ol></td>
    <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<p><span style=3D"color:#0055cc;"><strong>VARIABLES: </strong>List of Walk-=
me variables available for setting up segmentation rules under Walk-me edit=
or</span></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong><span><span>1.FIRM TYPE VARIABLES:</span></span></strong><span><=
span> (</span><span>walkme.firmType</span><span>)</span></span></p>
<p><span><span>IB, Internal, PM, NBIN, IFM, OT (without single or double qu=
otes)</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span><span>Internal: </span><span>NBIN Demo firm is COR </span><span>(o=
nly demo accounts, not prod data)&nbsp;</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p=
>
<p><span><span>NBIN: </span><span>NBIN </span><span>internal&nbsp; is</span=
><span> NBIN</span><span> (</span><span>access to all RR code ranges and </=
span><span>access to prod data)</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong><span><span>2. FIRM VARIABLES</span><span> </span></span></stron=
g><span><span>(</span><span>walkme.firm</span><span>)</span></span></p>
<p><span><span>Value is the firm code (without single or double quotes)</sp=
an></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p><span><strong>3.</strong>&nbsp;</span><strong style=3D"letter-spacing: 0=
.0px;">FEATURE VARIABLES&nbsp;</strong></p>
